      "failingExample": "Bug condition exploration test FAILED as expected (6 bug-condition assertions failed, 4 preservation assertions passed). Counterexamples found:\n\nBUG 1.1 (deep nested path not rewritten): build.js rewriteHtml regex `href=\"(?:\\.\\.\\/|\\/)?styles\\.css\"` only matches 0 or 1 `../` prefix.\n  - Input: `<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../../styles.css\">` → actual output: unchanged (`../../styles.css` survives), expected: `/static/styles.<hash>.css`\n  - Input: `<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../../../styles.css\">` → actual: unchanged, expected: rewritten\n  - Input: `<script src=\"../../script.js\" defer></script>` → actual: unchanged, expected: `/static/script.<hash>.js`\n  Note: no current page uses ../../ paths (diagnostic/start and tools/author-geo-audit use /styles.css root-relative), so the bug is latent in the regex but demonstrable via direct testing.\n\nBUG 1.2 (intake page missing script tag): Intake/amazon-visibility.html has no `<script src=\"...script.js\">` element — only Plausible analytics and inline form scripts. No client-side JS runs on that page.\n\nBUG 1.3 (Netlify post-processing flags enabled): netlify.toml sets `[build.processing.css] bundle = true`, `[build.processing.js] bundle = true`, and `[build.processing.html] pretty_urls = true`, bypassing immutable /static/* cache headers.\n\nPRESERVATION (confirmed working): single-level `../styles.css`, root-relative `/styles.css`, and bare `styles.css` all rewrite correctly. Built dist/Intake/amazon-visibility.html correctly references hashed /static/styles.<hash>.css.",
