    "3. Write bug condition exploration test for Backend / Agent Service Bugs": {
      "status": "passed",
      "failingExample": "Bug condition exploration test FAILED as expected (8 bug-condition tests fail, 4 preservation tests pass). Counterexamples found:\n\n1. Bug 1.11 (Stale Assertion): test-comprehensive.js contains `repB.critical_failures.some(f => f.includes('llms.txt'))` — asserts llms.txt in critical_failures, but scanner treats llms.txt as optional.\n\n2. Bug 1.12 (Redundant DNS, ~9 lookups): safeFetch calls `validateSSRF(currentUrl)` directly (1 DNS lookup) AND uses `ssrfSafeAgent` with `guardedLookup` (1 DNS lookup) = 2 per fetch. scanWithContent also calls `validateSSRF(urlToScan)` directly = 1 + 4*(1+1) = 9 DNS lookups per hostname per scan.\n\n3. Bug 1.13 (Double-Fetch): runDiagnostic calls `scanner.runScan(url)` (fetches homepage/robots/llms/sitemap) then `crawlSite(scan.url, options)` which independently re-fetches the same 4 resources — each fetched twice.\n\n4. Bug 1.14 (Missing OWNER_EMAIL Guard): sendDraftEmail guard is `if (!process.env.RESEND_API_KEY)` and sendErrorEmail guard is the same — neither checks `!OWNER_EMAIL`. When OWNER_EMAIL is unset, `to: OWNER_EMAIL` is undefined, causing Resend API error. Compare: sendLeadNotification and sendDiagnosticOwnerNotice correctly check `!process.env.RESEND_API_KEY || !OWNER_EMAIL`.\n\nPreservation baseline confirmed: sendLeadNotification and sendDiagnosticOwnerNotice both guard both env vars; scanner exports scanWithContent; analyzeFiles sets checks.llms_txt=true when present.",
